import lib/graphics.dl
import tests/games/three_dimensional.dl

function position the camera from {spatial camera:view} in {graphics frame:frame}:
    execute:
        reset the camera in frame
        rotate the camera in frame by (0.0 - view's yaw) degrees around x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
        move the camera in frame by x (0.0 - view's position's x), y (0.0 - view's position's y) and z (0.0 - view's position's z)

function draw a cube at {spatial position:position} with size {floating-point number:size} in {graphics frame:frame}:
    execute:
        set half to (size / 2.0)
        save the model transform in frame
        move the model in frame by x position's x, y position's y and z position's z
        start triangles in frame

        use vertex color red 220, green 80 and blue 80 in frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z half to frame

        use vertex color red 80, green 220 and blue 80 in frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame

        use vertex color red 80, green 80 and blue 220 in frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame

        use vertex color red 220, green 220 and blue 80 in frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame

        use vertex color red 220, green 80 and blue 220 in frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y half and z (0.0 - half) to frame

        use vertex color red 80, green 220 and blue 220 in frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z (0.0 - half) to frame
        add a vertex at x half, y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame
        add a vertex at x (0.0 - half), y (0.0 - half) and z half to frame

        finish triangles in frame
        restore the model transform in frame

set window to a new window with width 800 and height 600

set view to a camera at (a position with x 0.0, y 1.5 and z 8.0) facing 0.0 degrees with speed 0.2 and turn rate 2.0

while window remains open:
    if key (the up arrow key) is down in window:
        decrease the x coordinate of view's position by ((the sine of (view's yaw * 0.0174533)) * view's movement)
        decrease the z coordinate of view's position by ((the cosine of (view's yaw * 0.0174533)) * view's movement)
    if key (the down arrow key) is down in window:
        increase the x coordinate of view's position by ((the sine of (view's yaw * 0.0174533)) * view's movement)
        increase the z coordinate of view's position by ((the cosine of (view's yaw * 0.0174533)) * view's movement)
    if key (the right arrow key) is down in window:
        add view's turning to view's yaw
    if key (the left arrow key) is down in window:
        subtract view's turning from view's yaw

    set frame to a new graphics frame in window with background red (20.0 / 255.0), green (26.0 / 255.0), blue (36.0 / 255.0) and alpha 1.0
    use perspective with a vertical field of view of 77.3 degrees, a near plane of 0.1 and a far plane of 200.0 in frame
    enable depth testing in frame
    position the camera from view in frame
    draw a cube at (a position with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) with size 2.0 in frame
    display frame

close the window
